<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cartography">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cartography</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cartography is the science and art of making maps. Portuguese navigators of the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries greatly expanded European geographical knowledge and charts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> cartography, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a>, advanced substantially through the demands of managing the global trade of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p></div>
